   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription A 25-year-old student from Khammam in Telangana, Nallamala Akshita, died of a suspected heart attack in Albany, New York, U.S., on October 23, according to sources. Daughter of Khammam-based trader Nallamala Anand, Askhita moved to the U.S. four years ago for higher education. Meanwhile, BRS senior leader and former Khammam MP Nama Nageswara Rao expressed his condolences to her family over her untimely death.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅A即可解锁。据消息人士称，来自特伦甘纳邦卡马姆的25岁学生纳拉姆拉拉·阿克希塔于10月23日在美国纽约州奥尔巴尼因疑似心脏病发作去世。卡马姆商人纳拉姆拉拉·阿南德之女阿克希塔四年前赴美接受高等教育。与此同时，人民宗教党（BRP）高级领导人、前卡马姆议员纳马·纳格什瓦拉·劳向其家人致以慰问，祝愿她因过早去世而离世。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription A 25-year-old student from Khammam in Telangana, Nallamala Akshita, died of a suspected heart attack in Albany, New York, U.S., on October 23, according to sources. Daughter of Khammam-based trader Nallamala Anand, Askhita moved to the U.S. four years ago for higher education. She recently completed her Master of Science (MS) degree and had been looking for job opportunities. Her sudden death has left her family devastated, shattering their hopes for her future. Meanwhile, BRS senior leader and former Khammam MP Nama Nageswara Rao expressed his condolences to her family over her untimely death. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
