   "title": "State Police: Yobe Assembly Approves Constitutional Amendment",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/state-police-yobe-assembly-approves-constitutional-amendment/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:51:17 +0000",
   "_dt": 1792709477.0,
   "ageDays": 1.79,
   "summary": "The approval followed deliberations by lawmakers on 26 proposed constitutional amendment bills transmitted by the National Assembly to state legislatures for consideration and voting. Under the constitutional amendment process, proposed alterations require the approval of at least two-thirds of the state Houses of Assembly to meet the relevant legislative requirement.",
   "summary_zh": "此次批准之前，议员们审议了国民议会提交各州立法机构考虑和表决的26项拟议宪法修正案法案。按照宪法修正程序，拟议修改须获得至少三分之二州议会批准，方可达到相关立法要求。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The approval followed deliberations by lawmakers on 26 proposed constitutional amendment bills transmitted by the National Assembly to state legislatures for consideration and voting. Speaking on the resolutions, the Speaker of the House, Alhaji Chiroma Buba Mashio, said the bills were forwarded to state legislatures to enable them to consider and vote on the proposed amendments in line with constitutional requirements. Mashio explained that the proposal for State Police was aimed at providing a constitutional framework for states to establish their own police services. He said the proposal formed part of ongoing national discussions on security sector reform, particularly efforts to strengthen the country’s capacity to address emerging security challenges. The 26 proposed constitutional alteration bills seek amendments to various provisions of the 1999 Constitution of the Federal Republic of Nigeria. Under the constitutional amendment process, proposed alterations require the approval of at least two-thirds of the state Houses of Assembly to meet the relevant legislative requirement. The Yobe Assembly’s approval represents the state’s position on the proposal, while its implementation depends on the completion of the constitutionally prescribed amendment process. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel --> --> Jibril Mohammed Nabil Jibril Mohammed Nabil is a Reporter with Leadership Newspaper, covering Yobe State, specialising in education, health, security, technology, and human-angle stories. He holds a Master's degree in Communication Studies from Bayero University, Kano, and is known for well-researched, in-depth reporting and a commitment to accuracy that has established him as a reliable voice in his areas of coverage",
