   "published": "Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:32:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1792679523.0,
   "ageDays": 2.14,
   "summary": "South Korea and the United States on Thursday held joint river-crossing drills aimed at enhancing interoperability as part of the annual Hoguk military exercise, the South Korean Army said. Some 540 troops from the allies took part in the drills along the Namhan River in Yeoju, about 65 kilometers southeast of Seoul. Gen. Robert Brown, commanding general of the 2nd Infantry Division/South Korea-U.S. Combined Division, observed the drills",
   "summary_zh": "韩国军方表示，韩国和美国于周四举行联合渡河演练，旨在提高两军协同作战能力。此次演练是年度“护国”军事演习的一部分，约540名两军人员参加，演练地点位于首尔东南约65公里的礼城南汉江一带。韩国陆军第2步兵师／韩美联合师司令罗伯特·布朗将军视察了演练。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "South Korea and the United States on Thursday held joint river-crossing drills aimed at enhancing interoperability as part of the annual Hoguk military exercise, the South Korean Army said. Some 540 troops from the allies took part in the drills along the Namhan River in Yeoju, about 65 kilometers southeast of Seoul. The drills mobilized some 130 pieces of equipment, including 10 KM3 amphibious bridging vehicles, ribbon bridge systems and about 50 combat vehicles, such as K2 tanks and K21 armored vehicles. During the drills, the allied forces jointly installed and crossed a bridge spanning a 280-meter section of the river. Army Chief of Staff Gen. Kim Gyu-ha and U.S. Brig. Gen. Robert Brown, commanding general of the 2nd Infantry Division/South Korea-U.S. Combined Division, observed the drills",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
