   "title": "S. Korean, US air forces to bolster autonomous combat platform cooperation",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/defense/20261022/s-korean-us-air-forces-to-bolster-autonomous-combat-platform-cooperation",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:32:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1792679523.0,
   "ageDays": 2.14,
   "summary": "The air forces of Korea and the United States will sign a letter of intent (LOI) on autonomous combat platform cooperation Thursday to bolster collaboration in the manned-unmanned combat systems, the Korean Air Force said. The LOI will be signed during a meeting between the chiefs of staff of the two countries' air forces — Gen. Son Sug-rag and U.S. Gen. Kenneth Wilsbach, the South's armed force said in a statement.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国空军表示，韩国和美国空军将于星期四签署一份关于自主作战平台合作的意向书，以加强双方在有人—无人作战系统方面的协作。韩国武装力量部队在一份声明中说，这份意向书将在两国空军参谋长举行会议期间签署，签署方为孙锡乐上将和美国肯尼斯·威尔斯巴赫上将。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The air forces of Korea and the United States will sign a letter of intent (LOI) on autonomous combat platform cooperation Thursday to bolster collaboration in the manned-unmanned combat systems, the Korean Air Force said. The LOI will be signed during a meeting between the chiefs of staff of the two countries' air forces — Gen. Son Sug-rag and U.S. Gen. Kenneth Wilsbach, the South's armed force said in a statement. The autonomous collaborative platform (ACP) refers to an autonomous system designed to collaborate with manned aircraft and other unmanned assets to execute air missions. Such manned-unmanned teaming (MUM-T) is regarded as a cornerstone of next-generation air operations, reducing risks to pilots and significantly boosting the operational range and survival chances for airmen. The collaboration comes as the U.S. Air Force is pushing for the development and operational integration of the unmanned combat aircraft systems. Korea's Air Force is also working to lay the groundwork to secure operational capabilities for the MUM-T systems. Building on the collaboration, the two air forces plan to bolster cooperation to advance operational concepts and interoperability for future MUM-T combat systems, the Air Force said",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
