   "title": "After Shivamogga Dasara incident, PETA India offers mechanical elephants to Karnataka",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/bangalore/after-shivamogga-dasara-incident-peta-india-offers-mechanical-elephants-to-karnataka/article71611989.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:56:18 +0530",
   "_dt": 1792679178.0,
   "ageDays": 2.14,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription In a letter to Forest, Ecology, and Environment Minister Ramalinga Reddy, PETA India requested the State government to make this the last Dasara to feature live elephants and send captive elephants to sanctuaries where they can live unchained.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁。PETA India在致森林、生态与环境部长拉马林加·雷迪的信中，请求邦政府让今年成为最后一个仍 featuring 活象的达萨拉节，并将圈养象送往它们可以不受锁链束缚地生活的保护区。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription In a letter to Forest, Ecology, and Environment Minister Ramalinga Reddy, PETA India requested the State government to make this the last Dasara to feature live elephants and send captive elephants to sanctuaries where they can live unchained. “Mechanical elephants, which can move their heads, ears, eyes, trunks, and tails, are mounted on wheeled bases and can carry ceremonial idols during processions and rituals, offering an alternative to the use of live animals,” PETA India suggested. The request came after the Jamboo Savari procession, held as part of the Dasara celebrations in Shivamogga on Wednesday, witnessed scary scenes when the elephant carrying the howdah ran helter-skelter within minutes of the procession kicking off. The incident is the latest episode, with similar incidents reported during Dasara celebrations and at elephant camps in the State. In October 2021, elephant Gopalaswamy panicked during the Srirangapatna Dasara after being startled by firecrackers. This had prompted organisers to cancel the elephant procession, and the idol of Goddess Chamundeshwari was instead carried on a silver chariot. In September 2024, elephants Dhananjaya and Kanjan fought inside the palace grounds in Mysuru, sending Kanjan fleeing onto a busy road as onlookers ran for safety. Earlier this year, Kanjan fought with another captive elephant, Marthanda, at Dubare Elephant Camp in Kodagu. A woman tourist was crushed to death in the confrontation, while Marthanda died of his injuries the following day. PETA India Vice-President of Policy Khushboo Gupta said Dasara’s message of the triumph of good over evil should extend to the treatment of animals. “No elephant should be made to suffer or put people’s lives at risk in the name of celebration, especially now that mechanical elephants exist,” she said, adding that the organisation was ready to help the State make the transition. The request comes after Karnataka got its 11th mechanical elephant facilitated by PETA India and Compassion Unlimited Plus Action (CUPA). Named Shivayogiswara, the life-size mechanical elephant was donated to DMS Chandravana Ashrama in Mandya and unveiled on Wednesday. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "in"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_thehindu",
   "title_zh": "希瓦莫加达萨拉事件后，印度PETA向卡纳塔克邦提供机械象",
   "body_zh": "订阅账户还可享受《The Hindu》深度报道、社论、观点等更多内容。订阅即可解锁这些内容。在致信森林、生态与环境部长拉马林加·雷迪时，印度 PETA 请求邦政府确保今年十胜节是最后一个出现活象的节日，并将圈养大象送往保护中心，让它们在那里不受锁链束缚地生活。印度 PETA 建议：“机械象可以活动头部、耳朵、眼睛、鼻子和尾巴，安装在带轮底座上，能够在游行和宗教仪式中驮载仪式神像，为使用活体动物提供了一种替代方案。”此前，星期三在希瓦莫加举行的十胜节庆祝活动包含 Jambo Savari 游行；游行开始后不到几分钟，驮载象轿的大象便惊慌失控，引发令人惊恐的场面。这起事件只是最新的一例；十胜节庆祝活动期间以及该邦的大象营地此前也报告过类似事件。2021 年 10 月，大象 Gopalaswamy 在斯里兰加帕特纳十胜节期间受到鞭炮惊吓后陷入恐慌。这促使活动组织者取消了大象游行，女神 Chamundeshwari 的神像改由一辆银色战车承载。2024 年 9 月，大象 Dhananjaya 和 Kanjan 在迈索尔宫殿院内争斗，Kanjan 逃上繁忙道路，围观者则奔向安全地带。今年早些时候，Kanjan 在科达格的 Dubare 大象营地与另一头圈养大象 Marthanda 争斗。一名女性游客在冲突中被碾压身亡，Marthanda 也在次日因伤死亡。印度 PETA 政策副总裁 Khushboo Gupta 表示，十胜节所传达的善战胜恶的精神也应当延伸至动物待遇。她说：“不应让任何大象以庆典之名遭受痛苦或使人们的生命面临风险，尤其是在机械象已经存在的情况下。”她还补充，该组织愿意协助邦政府完成这一转变。此前，在印度 PETA 与 Compassion Unlimited Plus Action（CUPA）的协助下，卡纳塔克邦迎来了第 11 头机械象。这头与真象大小相同的机械象名为 Shivayogiswara，捐赠给曼迪亚的 DMS Chandravana Ashrama，并于星期三揭幕。评论必须使用英文，并以完整句子表述。评论不得包含辱骂性或针对个人的内容。请遵守我们的社区评论准则。我们已迁移至新的评论平台。如果你已是《The Hindu》注册用户并已登录，可以继续参与我们的文章讨论。如果你没有账户，请注册并登录后发表评论。用户登录自己的账户后，可以在 Vuukle 上查看过去的评论。"
