   "title": "U.S. Ambassador to South Korea Michelle Steel said: “South Korea is no longer a country that simply relies on U.S. protection.” She criticiz",
   "url": "https://x.com/monarchreport25/status/2113092618863415466",
   "snippet": "U.S. Ambassador to South Korea Michelle Steel said: “South Korea is no longer a country that simply relies on U.S. protection.”\n\nShe criticized the lack of a level playing field for American companies, pointing to raids, audits, and fines in the digital sector, and described the relationship as “turbulence.”\n\nThis goes beyond protecting U.S. firms. \n\nUnder the Lee Jae-myung administration, pressure linking the Coupang case to intelligence sharing and security talks has grown, and Steel is openly pushing South Korea to move from being protected to sharing the burden.\n\nIf U.S. deterrence weakens, the costs of dealing with China and North Korea will fall more directly on South Korea. Her remarks are essentially a call to reallocate that burden.\n\nSource: KBS",
   "body": "U.S. Ambassador to South Korea Michelle Steel said: “South Korea is no longer a country that simply relies on U.S. protection.”\n\nShe criticized the lack of a level playing field for American companies, pointing to raids, audits, and fines in the digital sector, and described the relationship as “turbulence.”\n\nThis goes beyond protecting U.S. firms. \n\nUnder the Lee Jae-myung administration, pressure linking the Coupang case to intelligence sharing and security talks has grown, and Steel is openly pushing South Korea to move from being protected to sharing the burden.\n\nIf U.S. deterrence weakens, the costs of dealing with China and North Korea will fall more directly on South Korea. Her remarks are essentially a call to reallocate that burden.\n\nSource: KBS",
